ut, then append the input to the div. So the DOM order becomes: ... container div (with input inside), then after the container? Actually the container div is before the input, and input is inside it. So after the input, there is nothing else inside the container except maybe the ul and status which are appended inside container as well (inside: this.container). So the container's children: input, ul, status (in that order they were appended). So after the input, the ul is next sibling. Then inside ul, the li items.

Thus Tab from input will go to the first focusable element after input: that is the ul? ul is not focusable unless given tabindex. It doesn't have tabindex. Then the li items have tabindex=0, so the first li gets focus. That matches observed behavior: focus moved to first li item.

